1
00:00:06,172 --> 00:00:07,966
[birds chirping]

2
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,467
[girl] <i>Nimuel, where are we going?</i>

3
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:13,054
Just follow me, Clara. I saw it down here.

4
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:17,976
Hurry up!

5
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:24,816
Come on, it's just over here.

6
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:29,237
[water splashing]

7
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:39,497
[Nimuel] You see that boat?

8
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:41,166
It looks weird, hey?

9
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,335
Come on, let's take a look.

10
00:00:57,974 --> 00:00:58,808
Watch your step.

11
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:01,811
[Nimuel pants]

12
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:15,867
[Nimuel groans]

13
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,661
Come on, you check over there.

14
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:29,881
[Nimuel grunts]

15
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:34,469
Clara, do you think this can fly?

16
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:36,846
[Clara] Maybe.

17
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,181
Whoa, look at this.

18
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:40,016
[chuckles]

19
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:57,242
- [engine starts]
- [Clara shrieks]

20
00:01:58,201 --> 00:01:59,410
[engine shuts off]

21
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:01,704
[Nimuel] Clara?

22
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,039
Clara?

23
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:04,707
Clara!

24
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:06,251
Clara!

25
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:08,962
Clara!

26
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:12,841
Clara! [echoes]

27
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:16,219
[theme music playing]

28
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:22,452
BALARAW: BLOOD ISLAND

29
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:39,302
[recorder whirring]

30
00:03:41,554 --> 00:03:43,765
[classical music playing]

31
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,366
[wind blowing]

32
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:04,244
[music continues playing]

33
00:04:16,756 --> 00:04:19,133
[birds chirping]

34
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:41,155
[music stops]

35
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:56,838
[scoffs] Well, who would have thought
maybe that could work for me?

36
00:04:56,921 --> 00:04:59,299
[laughs]

37
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:03,636
How long has Mom really been gone?

38
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:07,181
Well, like I told you yesterday--

39
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:08,933
I want the truth, okay? Don't lie.

40
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,560
She's been gone a long time.

41
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:11,602
It changes nothing.

42
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:14,063
- It changes a lot for me.
- [bangs table]

43
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:17,025
We just didn't want to worry you, okay?

44
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:20,445
Yes. Rebecca has been missing
for a few weeks.

45
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:23,323
I wouldn't be surprised if she was dead.

46
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:25,366
[shushes] Javier!

47
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:27,827
- Am I wrong?
- [Ramon sighs]

48
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:29,329
And which way did she go?

49
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:33,207
- Are you gonna go after her?
- She's my mom.

50
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:35,877
- Of course I'm gonna look for her.
- Sabina, hold on.

51
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,505
I'm telling you this right now.

52
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:40,673
It's dangerous out there.

53
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:43,342
- You could die, you know.
- Yeah, I'm still going.

54
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,432
- [birds chirping]
- [water dripping]

55
00:05:50,224 --> 00:05:51,434
[Arturo] Rebecca, tell me.

56
00:05:58,483 --> 00:05:59,484
[Arturo sighs]

57
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:02,320
Have you done what you came here for?

58
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:04,530
[Rebecca sniffles]

59
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:13,664
[lighter clicks]

60
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:15,291
It's dry now.

61
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:20,213
But only got one left.

62
00:06:21,672 --> 00:06:23,174
- They're all gone.
- [lighter clicks]

63
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:27,970
[Arturo groans]

64
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,183
[Arturo exhales]

65
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:52,787
When I came here,

66
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:58,167
first I went to the camp
where they were holding my brother…

67
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:01,629
but Ramon's men caught me.

68
00:07:05,174 --> 00:07:06,551
Did you at least find Vedasto?

69
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:09,095
It wasn't easy.

70
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:13,432
You know, you can't save the unwilling.

71
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:18,563
What do you mean by "unwilling"?

72
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:23,484
[sighs] My brother's alive,

73
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,487
but he's no longer himself.

74
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:30,658
I don't know what happened
or what they did to him.

75
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:37,415
But you know what?

76
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:39,500
Now I just want to be free of this place.

77
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,169
But now I can't do that.

78
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:43,379
Because now…

79
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:47,675
there's something else to worry about:
you guys.

80
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:50,678
You shouldn't have come here.

81
00:07:52,054 --> 00:07:52,889
Remember?

82
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:55,391
You promised
you wouldn't let Sabina find me.

83
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:56,601
She shouldn't be here.

84
00:07:57,226 --> 00:08:00,021
Hey, there was nothing we could tell her
that would make her stay.

85
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:01,439
[Rebecca scoffs]

86
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:02,773
You know what she's like.

87
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,985
The only options were either
to go with her or get left behind.

88
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:09,363
And you know what?

89
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:10,948
I couldn't do that to Sabina.

90
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:14,660
So now…

91
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:18,539
We <i>all</i> need to get off this damn island.

92
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:20,791
But how?

93
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:25,630
Our problem now is finding Sabina.

94
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:30,676
- [water dripping]
- [distant creaking]

95
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:33,221
[creaking, soft thud]

96
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:48,653
Sarge?

97
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:13,553
How long you been awake?

98
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:17,056
I've been awake for about an hour,
I guess.

99
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:18,766
This one.

100
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:22,353
- I doubt she's even blinked.
- [gun cocks]

101
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:24,689
She's certainly not herself,
that's for sure.

102
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:29,402
I wouldn't be either
if I'd been stuck on this island.

103
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:31,571
Ehh…

104
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:34,240
Yeah, you wouldn't last a day.

105
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:36,993
And what would you know?

106
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:37,910
[gun cocks]

107
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:49,380
I told Ramon I don't need anything to eat.

108
00:09:49,463 --> 00:09:50,298
This is from me.

109
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:52,633
Take it for your journey.

110
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,403
Is it really dangerous where I'm going?

111
00:10:13,362 --> 00:10:14,989
Your father wasn't lying to you.

112
00:10:16,073 --> 00:10:18,659
[Sabina] Well, he did lie to me
about my mother, didn't he?

113
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:21,037
Only to protect you, yes.

114
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:23,623
The Cardomas just want to protect us.

115
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:26,000
You think it's true,
all the stuff they're saying?

116
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:29,045
That I'll meet my death
on the other side of the island?

117
00:10:30,087 --> 00:10:30,921
It's true.

118
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,844
From my experience,
not everything ends in death.

119
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:42,141
[panting]

120
00:10:45,686 --> 00:10:48,105
[whimpering]

121
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,944
[sobbing]

122
00:10:56,989 --> 00:11:00,534
Señor, please.
Ramon, please just bury her.

123
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:04,080
[cries] Not my Clara, please, no.

124
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,499
[continues sobbing]

125
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:16,050
[Ramon] Sabina,
you said you were a nurse, right?

126
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:17,510
Something's happened.

127
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:20,304
We need your help.
One of our men is wounded.

128
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:23,265
If you're able to help him,
we'll help find your mother.

129
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:25,893
Okay.

130
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:27,686
But she comes with me.

131
00:11:31,273 --> 00:11:32,191
[Ramon] Follow me.

132
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:48,040
[Rebecca] They're here.

133
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:50,501
Including the brothers.

134
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:53,796
You mean the brothers
who are running this whole place?

135
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:54,964
Mm-hmm.

136
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:56,674
The ones that took your brother captive?

137
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:59,176
[Ramon] Crisanto, where's Atoy?

138
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,512
[Crisanto] Most likely alive
but wounded, señor.

139
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:04,265
There's a trail of blood
going into the jungle.

140
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:23,576
What do you want me to do?

141
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:25,536
I want you to help.

142
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:29,999
[Javier] You and I both know who did this.

143
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:33,169
And she's probably aiming
a gun at us right now.

144
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,045
Why did you bring the girl along?

145
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:36,213
We're sitting ducks out here.

146
00:12:36,297 --> 00:12:38,257
We should go back
to the houses straight away.

147
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:41,010
You damn dog, Ramon!

148
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:43,554
What's happening down there?

149
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:46,807
[Rebecca sighs]

150
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:48,476
He knows I won't shoot if Sabina's there.

151
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:52,396
[Ramon] How do you think that we've
been here this long and we're still alive?

152
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:58,068
Now you know why I brought the girl along.

153
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:02,698
- Let's go.
- [Arturo] What is it?

154
00:13:08,078 --> 00:13:09,079
[Rebecca] I need a new plan.

155
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:14,877
[Arturo] So where do those brothers live,
huh? Let's ambush them.

156
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,836
I bet I could take them

157
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:21,717
An animal didn't do this.

158
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:27,389
A lot of strange things
can pass as animals.

159
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:29,725
Let's go find Atoy.

160
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:35,731
Crisanto, any sign of him?

161
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:40,236
[Crisanto] Atoy has made it a long way,
señor.

162
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:41,779
He's still young and strong.

163
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,406
There is a limit to one's strength.

164
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:47,243
Are we near to the place
where my mom went?

165
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,828
[Crisanto] No, not even close.

166
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:53,582
My wife and I were born here.

167
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:56,961
We know this island
like the back of our hands,

168
00:13:57,878 --> 00:14:00,506
but even we lose our way
from time to time.

169
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:04,051
It's very dangerous to wander here alone,

170
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:06,303
especially for newcomers.

171
00:14:07,346 --> 00:14:09,473
You said that no one
who arrives here can ever leave.

172
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:11,475
Your mother managed it, though.

173
00:14:12,309 --> 00:14:13,394
I don't know how she did it.

174
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:14,979
We can never leave by boat.

175
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:17,147
The tide seems to have a mind of its own.

176
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:21,860
What, you think we didn't try?

177
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,822
Well, I suppose then I can't leave either.

178
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:27,366
I don't know.
I guess you better find your mother.

179
00:14:27,449 --> 00:14:29,201
You can ask her how she managed it.

180
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,329
You may be able to leave Balaraw,

181
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:34,915
but you can never escape it.

182
00:14:41,755 --> 00:14:43,757
[female voice] <i>Sabina!</i>

183
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,762
<i>Sabina!</i>

184
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:53,100
<i>- Sabina!</i>
- [fluttering]

185
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:11,535
So, what do we do now, Aunt Becca?

186
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:13,537
[Rebecca] We keep trying to work out
how to rescue Sabina.

187
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,873
- [line ringing]
- [Arturo] Hey, look, I got signal.

188
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:18,334
- [Bulak] Let me see.
- Yeah, one bar.

189
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:21,170
- Elias! Elias!
- [Elias] <i>Is that you?</i>

190
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:22,713
<i>Where are you? You're breaking up.</i>

191
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:26,383
We're in the island, Babang Yawa.
We found Rebecca.

192
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:29,178
- [Elias] <i>Say again.</i>
- Can you read me? We found Rebecca.

193
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:30,095
[static]

194
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,764
[unintelligible transmission]

195
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:33,390
[static crackling]

196
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,773
[Sabina exhales]

197
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,527
[twigs snap]

198
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:53,661
[female voice] <i>Sabina.</i>

199
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:59,375
[voice grows louder] <i>Sabina.</i>

200
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:04,213
<i>Sabina.</i>

201
00:16:04,296 --> 00:16:06,548
[breathing heavily]

202
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:10,552
<i>Sabina, I've been waiting for you.</i>

203
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:12,972
<i>One must remain,</i>

204
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:17,559
<i>and one shall be sacrificed.</i>

205
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:20,854
[whimpers]

206
00:16:23,607 --> 00:16:25,943
[panting]

207
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:29,780
[gasps] Señora, where did you go?

208
00:16:29,863 --> 00:16:30,948
[Sabina pants]

209
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:32,908
Diwa, I heard something. Did you?

210
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:35,911
Come with me. It's not far from here.

211
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:37,162
We don't go down there.

212
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:42,292
[female voice] <i>Sabina.</i>

213
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:47,214
<i>Sabina.</i>

214
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:50,926
[Rebecca sighs]

215
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:53,220
I just can't shake this feeling.

216
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:56,223
This place isn't right. It's evil.

217
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:02,021
It's like it has a mind of its own,
a life of its own.

218
00:17:04,314 --> 00:17:05,149
It's watching.

219
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,901
Like it has its own voice.

220
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,319
A beating heart.

221
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:10,237
Maybe a brain too.

222
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:14,825
Is he still breathing? He looks pale.

223
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:17,619
Where's Sabina?

224
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:20,622
[Diwa] You all walk too fast, señor.

225
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:22,374
Your daughter's not used to the island.

226
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,543
He's losing a lot of blood.

227
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:27,046
Someone give me a tourniquet.
We need to stop the bleeding.

228
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,006
Can I use this, Crisanto?

229
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:34,803
Uh, it needs to be disinfected.

230
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:35,721
[Ramon] Here.

231
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:40,100
This one is very pure,
cleaner than alcohol.

232
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,233
- [Atoy groans]
- [Rebecca] Okay.

233
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:50,778
First thing I need
to slow down the flow of blood.

234
00:17:52,821 --> 00:17:54,156
That won't hold it for long.

235
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:56,075
We need to take him back to Raphael.

236
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,534
Well.

237
00:17:58,202 --> 00:17:59,036
You heard her.

238
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:04,208
Keep pressure on it.

239
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:09,463
Now, we're gonna be celebrating
Talas tonight.

240
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:11,548
[Rebecca] Put some pressure
on here and here. Hold it tight.

241
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:12,549
And with Sabina?

242
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:21,975
[Rebecca] Faster Crisanto.
He doesn't have a lot of time.

243
00:18:23,769 --> 00:18:26,730
[Javier] Let's hope we can still save him,
God willing.

244
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:30,984
[Diwa] We've lost so many of our family.

245
00:18:32,027 --> 00:18:33,737
Oh. Like who?

246
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:38,450
My daughter.

247
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:40,786
Clara.

248
00:18:48,836 --> 00:18:50,129
And Crisanto's wife.

249
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:52,381
Mina was lost.

250
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:55,759
Lost how?

251
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:01,598
My daughter's body…

252
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,059
She was found.

253
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:07,396
But we never found Mina.

254
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:08,313
She's gone.

255
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:10,566
Crisanto's wife.

256
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:18,949
I was lucky, you know.

257
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:24,413
Crisanto has had a harder time of it
than I have.

258
00:19:25,789 --> 00:19:27,749
He doesn't know if it's time to grieve…

259
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:31,545
or hope someday to find her.

260
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:40,804
That's as much as I can do for now.

261
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:43,140
He's already lost so much blood.

262
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:45,601
We'll monitor for a while.

263
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:47,936
I just hope we're not too late.

264
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:50,522
I hope so, too.

265
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:52,900
[crow cawing]

266
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:15,172
[birds chirping]

267
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,803
[fire crackling]

268
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:29,728
[woman sobbing softly]

269
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:37,236
Dying is a sad thing.

270
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:45,911
And that's what we usually focus on,
the sadness, grief, pain.

271
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:48,747
We feel what is lost.

272
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:53,627
Which means it's easy to forget
about the good times we shared…

273
00:20:56,171 --> 00:21:00,300
the happy times we had
with our dearly departed friends…

274
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:03,345
our family…

275
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:06,682
- and our loved ones.
- [woman continues sobbing]

276
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:08,433
You know,

277
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:11,812
whenever something
would break in our houses…

278
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:15,941
Talas is who we'd turn to.

279
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:21,405
That was Talas' gift to us:

280
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:23,198
support.

281
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,200
Service.

282
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:28,495
And home.

283
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:34,751
Now Talas is finally
going back to his true home.

284
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,338
And he's leaving for us…

285
00:21:42,426 --> 00:21:43,593
sustenance.

286
00:21:43,677 --> 00:21:44,845
[tense music playing]

287
00:21:44,928 --> 00:21:50,559
Food that may last for a week,
two weeks or even more.

288
00:21:51,476 --> 00:21:55,605
This is how we will celebrate
the wonderful life of Talas.

289
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:59,651
Talas, we are all indebted to you.

290
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:04,614
You have served us all so well,
you have been part of our family,

291
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:10,329
- and now I ask you for one last gift.
- [weapon unsheathes]

292
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:13,248
[whimpers]

293
00:22:15,125 --> 00:22:16,877
[breath trembling]

294
00:22:19,129 --> 00:22:21,298
- [gasps]
- [ominous music playing]

295
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:26,803
[flesh squelching]

296
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:28,347
[woman sobs]

297
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,609
[squelching]

298
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:47,157
[breath trembling]

299
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:15,936
[whimpers]

300
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:33,829
[Sabina breathing heavily]

301
00:23:41,628 --> 00:23:42,838
[Ramon] For you, Sabina.

302
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:53,557
[somber music playing]

303
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:10,532
[squelches]

304
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:17,706
[weapon clatters]

305
00:24:19,416 --> 00:24:20,250
[Diwa sniffles]

306
00:24:37,058 --> 00:24:38,518
[Ramon] As you were Clara's mother,

307
00:24:39,227 --> 00:24:41,396
do you receive this blessing first, Diwa?

308
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:54,826
[Sabina whimpering] Are you fucking crazy?

309
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:56,411
I am not eating that!

310
00:24:56,494 --> 00:24:57,329
Why?

311
00:24:57,412 --> 00:24:59,581
What do you think
you were eating yesterday with us?

312
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:07,505
[whimpers]

313
00:25:16,973 --> 00:25:18,350
[Diwa cries]

314
00:25:22,437 --> 00:25:24,147
[ominous music playing]

315
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:32,447
[Diwa sobs]

316
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:38,119
[dramatic music playing]

317
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,454
[Diwa pants]

318
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:44,042
[Diwa sobs]

319
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:47,337
[Sabina pants]

320
00:25:52,259 --> 00:25:53,969
[Diwa sobs]

321
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:17,575
[Sabina pants]

322
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,716
[soft thumping]

323
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:39,222
[grows louder]

324
00:27:24,893 --> 00:27:27,937
[female voice] <i>Sabina.</i>

325
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:30,023
Ma?

326
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:38,698
- [female voice] <i>Sabina.</i>
- [gasps]

327
00:28:09,813 --> 00:28:11,898
[ominous music continues]

328
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:21,658
[Rebecca]
<i>Are you still dreaming about the island?</i>

329
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:30,208
Ma?

330
00:28:31,292 --> 00:28:32,127
Ma!

331
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:35,880
Ma!

332
00:28:35,964 --> 00:28:37,382
[screams]

333
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:38,842
Ma!

334
00:28:38,925 --> 00:28:42,470
[Rebecca shrieks, screams]

335
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:44,472
[echoes]

336
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,474
[soft thumping continues, then stops]

337
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:50,186
[gasps]

338
00:28:57,318 --> 00:28:58,653
You should save your energy.

339
00:29:06,035 --> 00:29:07,120
Did you come from in there?

340
00:29:07,871 --> 00:29:09,873
[breathing heavily]

341
00:29:19,799 --> 00:29:20,633
[sighs]

342
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:23,136
You had us worried there.

343
00:29:24,929 --> 00:29:26,723
Why did you leave
in the middle of our feast?

344
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:28,600
[Sabina] Feast?

345
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:32,061
Do you even know
what you're saying anymore?

346
00:29:32,812 --> 00:29:35,565
[Javier] I don't expect you
to understand all at once.

347
00:29:36,316 --> 00:29:40,945
But whether you like it or not,
this is how we show respect to the body

348
00:29:41,029 --> 00:29:42,697
and life of those who've passed.

349
00:29:44,032 --> 00:29:46,785
You may not understand it,
but you must respect it.

350
00:29:48,411 --> 00:29:49,913
But I know you're new here.

351
00:29:51,122 --> 00:29:53,291
It may take you a while
to come to terms with it.

352
00:30:02,675 --> 00:30:04,886
What did you see
when you entered the jungle?

353
00:30:09,182 --> 00:30:11,267
[Ramon] Are you sure Atoy's not here?

354
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:14,062
[Diwa] Yes, señor, I'm sure.

355
00:30:16,773 --> 00:30:17,690
[indistinct chatter]

356
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:20,568
[Diwa] Is he a danger to us?

357
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:23,029
[Ramon] We will get through this.

358
00:30:25,448 --> 00:30:27,200
The Lord is watching over us.

359
00:30:33,832 --> 00:30:35,875
[distant rustling]

360
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:37,961
[suspenseful music playing]

361
00:30:40,421 --> 00:30:41,965
[rustling continues]

362
00:30:50,306 --> 00:30:52,517
[louder rustling]

363
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:00,108
[man screams]

364
00:31:00,984 --> 00:31:01,818
We must run!

365
00:31:02,485 --> 00:31:04,779
- We need to hurry!
- [man screams]

366
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:06,698
- What's happening?
- [Javier] Shut up! Come with me!

367
00:31:06,781 --> 00:31:07,782
[Crisanto] Run!

368
00:31:09,242 --> 00:31:10,118
Quickly! Go!

369
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:11,953
Hurry!

370
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:15,164
Run! Faster!

371
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:30,847
- [snarling]
- [squelching]

372
00:31:32,557 --> 00:31:33,433
[gasps]

373
00:31:35,351 --> 00:31:37,478
[grunting]

374
00:31:49,657 --> 00:31:50,491
[lighter clicks]

375
00:31:53,202 --> 00:31:56,247
I left the boat on the beach
about five miles to the north.

376
00:31:56,956 --> 00:31:58,291
I'm sure it's still there.

377
00:32:00,209 --> 00:32:02,003
Well, how can you be so sure?

378
00:32:02,086 --> 00:32:04,255
Those crazy people
could have found it and chopped it up?

379
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:06,215
Because I only just saw it.

380
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:10,261
I hid it very well behind the rocks.
They won't see it.

381
00:32:10,345 --> 00:32:12,555
[Arturo] Okay, so what's our plan
to get there?

382
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:16,059
[Rebecca] Okay. There's a hut
where they store all their food.

383
00:32:16,142 --> 00:32:18,853
If we can set fire to that,
we can create confusion,

384
00:32:19,646 --> 00:32:21,105
which will be the distraction we need

385
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:23,733
to break into the house and rescue Sabina.

386
00:32:25,443 --> 00:32:28,279
So, who torches the hut
and who breaks Sabina out?

387
00:32:33,534 --> 00:32:35,536
[pants] What the hell was that?

388
00:32:37,372 --> 00:32:39,374
It's better if Ramon explains it to you.

389
00:32:50,551 --> 00:32:52,553
Crisanto, was that Atoy?

390
00:32:53,554 --> 00:32:54,597
The one eating Kael.

391
00:32:59,143 --> 00:33:00,645
Kael had his orders.

392
00:33:01,437 --> 00:33:02,814
He was guarding the shore.

393
00:33:05,316 --> 00:33:06,693
No one should know this.

394
00:33:15,368 --> 00:33:17,620
The locals of this island are unique.

395
00:33:19,247 --> 00:33:22,917
If I hadn't managed to find a cure
for their illness, you know… [scoffs]

396
00:33:23,793 --> 00:33:25,586
Well, I think they all would have died.

397
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:26,504
What illness?

398
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:33,803
Whenever someone dies or gets sick,
or even gets injured in some way,

399
00:33:35,304 --> 00:33:37,140
they begin to transform.

400
00:33:38,683 --> 00:33:42,770
The only way to stop the transformation
is by eating the sacred meat.

401
00:33:43,646 --> 00:33:45,106
You'll understand eventually.

402
00:33:46,232 --> 00:33:47,483
We were just like you.

403
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:50,570
When we first arrived, it was a struggle.

404
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:54,073
You just need time to understand this.

405
00:33:55,241 --> 00:33:57,118
I've already had a lot of time to think.

406
00:33:57,201 --> 00:33:59,162
And there's one thing
that I'm certain about.

407
00:33:59,996 --> 00:34:01,330
You are not my father.

408
00:34:03,541 --> 00:34:05,918
There are no words
to explain what you are.

409
00:34:12,842 --> 00:34:14,093
As time goes by,

410
00:34:15,261 --> 00:34:18,181
I become more convinced
that, indeed, you are my daughter.

411
00:34:25,396 --> 00:34:26,314
[Arturo] Bear left here.

412
00:34:27,398 --> 00:34:29,025
[birds chirping]

413
00:34:31,652 --> 00:34:33,279
Are you sure this is the right direction?

414
00:34:34,614 --> 00:34:36,407
Well, Becca said this was the way.

415
00:34:42,538 --> 00:34:43,414
Hey, come on now.

416
00:34:43,915 --> 00:34:46,375
Hold your arms up,
and you'll get a better aim.

417
00:34:46,459 --> 00:34:48,920
I totally know what to do
with a gun, okay?

418
00:34:49,587 --> 00:34:51,547
[Arturo] Oh, yeah?
Did your drug dealer teach you?

419
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:53,424
[Bulak] No, it was your mother.

420
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:54,884
Hey, leave my mother out of this.

421
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:56,511
[crickets chirping]

422
00:35:00,181 --> 00:35:01,682
[whimpering]

423
00:35:07,021 --> 00:35:08,856
[children chattering distantly]

424
00:35:20,618 --> 00:35:21,452
[lighter clicks]

425
00:35:34,841 --> 00:35:37,009
[Javier] Crisanto,
no one's guarding the camp.

426
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:37,927
Hurry up!

427
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:07,331
[sinister music playing]

428
00:36:07,915 --> 00:36:08,749
Run!

429
00:36:16,382 --> 00:36:18,301
[panting]

430
00:36:50,291 --> 00:36:51,125
[door opens]

431
00:36:51,792 --> 00:36:52,919
- [boy laughs]
- [gasps]

432
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:55,588
[pants]

433
00:36:59,550 --> 00:37:02,345
[whimpers] There's someone inside!

434
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:04,013
There's someone in there!

435
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:14,315
[ominous music playing]

436
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:19,445
[creature gnawing]

437
00:37:21,864 --> 00:37:22,698
Who's there?

438
00:37:28,412 --> 00:37:30,539
[low growling]

439
00:37:38,339 --> 00:37:40,383
- [creature snarls]
- [Arturo screams]

440
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:45,137
- [growls]
- [screams]

441
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:46,514
[Bulak] Look out! [gasps]

442
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:48,891
[Arturo] Shoot it!

443
00:37:49,767 --> 00:37:52,520
Shoot it, Bulak! Shoot it. Now! Shoot!

444
00:37:57,942 --> 00:37:59,735
[dramatic drum beating]

445
00:38:05,074 --> 00:38:05,992
[distant gunshot]

446
00:38:08,661 --> 00:38:09,662
[gunshot]

447
00:38:11,747 --> 00:38:13,457
[rustling]

448
00:38:15,710 --> 00:38:17,712
[Arturo]
Fuck! What kind of monster was that?

449
00:38:19,255 --> 00:38:20,089
Where'd it go?

450
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:22,717
- [Ramon] What's happening?
- [man] Señor!

451
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:25,678
- Our food stores are burning!
- [Ramon] Quickly to the river!

452
00:38:25,761 --> 00:38:28,681
[people clamoring]

453
00:38:36,647 --> 00:38:37,857
- Stay here.
- Huh?

454
00:38:39,275 --> 00:38:41,610
Wait, what's happening?

455
00:38:41,694 --> 00:38:42,570
[lock clicks]

456
00:38:42,653 --> 00:38:43,487
Hey!

457
00:38:43,571 --> 00:38:46,365
- Sarge, is that a human or a fucking bat?
- I don't know what the hell that was.

458
00:38:46,449 --> 00:38:49,118
- And what's happened to Becca's diversion?
- We should run again, right?

459
00:38:49,201 --> 00:38:50,036
Great idea.

460
00:38:52,663 --> 00:38:55,207
[Crisanto] Señor,
someone set fire to our stores.

461
00:38:55,291 --> 00:38:57,001
Children said they saw a woman.

462
00:38:58,377 --> 00:38:59,211
Was it her?

463
00:39:00,212 --> 00:39:01,213
I think so.

464
00:39:01,297 --> 00:39:02,131
Then hurry.

465
00:39:03,924 --> 00:39:05,760
[Bulak] <i>Did you see how I shot</i>
<i>that monster, Sarge?</i>

466
00:39:05,843 --> 00:39:07,178
[Arturo] You didn't even come close.

467
00:39:08,095 --> 00:39:09,513
Hey, you smell that?

468
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:12,308
Way to go, Aunt Becca.

469
00:39:12,391 --> 00:39:14,018
[woman sobbing]

470
00:39:15,686 --> 00:39:16,854
[Arturo] There's our diversion.

471
00:39:16,937 --> 00:39:19,273
[people clamoring, crying]

472
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:21,692
[Arturo] We need to find the house
that Sabina's being kept in.

473
00:39:23,569 --> 00:39:24,403
You ready?

474
00:39:24,487 --> 00:39:25,488
Let's go.

475
00:39:30,159 --> 00:39:32,203
[Arturo] Hey, listen,
we don't want any trouble.

476
00:39:54,850 --> 00:39:56,310
[grunts] Help!

477
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:57,895
[rattling]

478
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:03,901
[grunts, pants]

479
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:16,122
[key rattling]

480
00:40:23,379 --> 00:40:24,213
Hurry!

481
00:40:25,756 --> 00:40:27,091
Señora, hurry! Leave it.

482
00:40:34,849 --> 00:40:35,683
[door closes]

483
00:40:35,766 --> 00:40:37,768
[tense music playing]

484
00:41:35,409 --> 00:41:37,828
Sarge, we need to find Sabina.

485
00:41:38,871 --> 00:41:39,705
Okay.

486
00:41:43,083 --> 00:41:44,877
[Andres] <i>No,</i>
<i>don't waste our drinking water.</i>

487
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,921
You need to get it
straight from the river.

488
00:41:47,004 --> 00:41:49,173
Now go! Hey! Get away from there!

489
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:51,008
Let it burn. It's gone.

490
00:41:51,091 --> 00:41:52,885
The flames will die down shortly.

491
00:41:52,968 --> 00:41:55,095
It's more important
to keep everybody safe.

492
00:41:56,263 --> 00:41:57,806
[breathing heavily]

493
00:41:58,599 --> 00:42:00,601
[Andres] Tell the others
to go get more water.

494
00:42:01,268 --> 00:42:04,188
That's all you could get?
You want us to starve, Crisanto?

495
00:42:04,271 --> 00:42:05,439
[Andres] Hurry up!

496
00:42:05,523 --> 00:42:07,024
Get more water from the river.

497
00:42:08,192 --> 00:42:10,945
I'm sorry. I did my best, but don't worry,

498
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:13,322
your brothers won't starve.

499
00:42:15,032 --> 00:42:17,034
[panting]

500
00:42:22,998 --> 00:42:25,417
[men grunting]

501
00:42:29,296 --> 00:42:31,048
[Javier] So we're just gonna stand here
and watch?

502
00:42:32,007 --> 00:42:33,717
[Ramon] The Lord will take care of us.

503
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:40,558
[men grunting]

504
00:42:42,476 --> 00:42:44,186
- This is as far as I can go.
- What?

505
00:42:44,270 --> 00:42:45,938
Just head straight
and you'll find the ocean.

506
00:42:46,522 --> 00:42:47,356
Come with me.

507
00:42:48,232 --> 00:42:49,066
I belong here.

508
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:50,901
I'm not like you.

509
00:42:52,444 --> 00:42:54,321
Diwa. Listen, okay?

510
00:42:54,405 --> 00:42:56,115
- There's more than just this island.
- Go, Sabina!

511
00:42:56,198 --> 00:42:57,741
- Run!
- You've got to get out of here.

512
00:42:57,825 --> 00:42:59,868
If you ever want to see your mother again,
you must go now.

513
00:42:59,952 --> 00:43:01,954
Please leave. Now, while you can.

514
00:43:06,625 --> 00:43:07,876
[ominous sting]

515
00:43:21,098 --> 00:43:22,766
[panting]

516
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:24,977
[footsteps running]

517
00:43:32,359 --> 00:43:33,360
[footsteps approaching]

518
00:43:35,863 --> 00:43:36,697
[groans]

519
00:43:37,990 --> 00:43:39,199
Where do you think you're going?

520
00:43:40,451 --> 00:43:42,077
You really think you'll get out of here?

521
00:43:42,161 --> 00:43:44,872
No, you'll rot on this island
like the rest of us.

522
00:43:46,915 --> 00:43:48,626
[Diwa gasps] Señor, please!

523
00:43:52,087 --> 00:43:53,380
Diwa, move aside.

524
00:43:55,674 --> 00:43:56,508
I said, move.

525
00:43:57,509 --> 00:43:58,802
Your choice, then.

526
00:43:58,886 --> 00:44:00,929
- [Diwa grunting]
- [gunshot]

527
00:44:05,017 --> 00:44:07,061
[grunts, cries]

528
00:44:10,481 --> 00:44:11,774
- [gunshot]
- [groans]

529
00:44:14,193 --> 00:44:16,236
You go check. I can handle it here.

530
00:44:20,532 --> 00:44:21,700
[groans]

531
00:44:23,243 --> 00:44:25,412
[Diwa gasping]

532
00:44:25,496 --> 00:44:28,540
[Sabina breathing heavily]

533
00:44:30,501 --> 00:44:32,628
Diwa, come with me.
Let Raphael see to this.

534
00:44:35,381 --> 00:44:36,674
[shuddering] This is all your fault.

535
00:44:37,716 --> 00:44:39,426
You ruined our lives.

536
00:44:41,845 --> 00:44:43,972
We lived peacefully before you came.

537
00:44:44,056 --> 00:44:47,393
Listen to me. You know what will happen
if Raphael doesn't see to you.

538
00:44:50,145 --> 00:44:51,980
You sure you're making the right decision?

539
00:44:56,110 --> 00:44:58,320
- Señor.
- Take these two and tie them up.

540
00:45:00,864 --> 00:45:02,032
Did you just do that to her?

541
00:45:02,116 --> 00:45:04,326
I wasn't aiming for her.
It was an accident.

542
00:45:04,410 --> 00:45:05,411
You gonna tie them up or not?

543
00:45:05,494 --> 00:45:08,163
Señor, please lower your gun.

544
00:45:08,247 --> 00:45:10,249
If I say do something, do it right away!

545
00:45:11,208 --> 00:45:12,835
You forget how to follow orders?

546
00:45:12,918 --> 00:45:14,920
Javier, what's this?

547
00:45:18,257 --> 00:45:19,883
What are you standing around for?

548
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:21,427
Send for Raphael quickly now.

549
00:45:21,510 --> 00:45:23,262
Sabina, come with me.

550
00:45:24,638 --> 00:45:25,514
You hear me?

551
00:45:25,597 --> 00:45:26,807
Get up and come with me now.

552
00:45:29,643 --> 00:45:30,561
Señor, no!

553
00:45:31,186 --> 00:45:33,272
I said get up
and come with me straight away.

554
00:45:33,355 --> 00:45:34,189
No.

555
00:45:34,940 --> 00:45:36,650
- Señor!
- [Andres] Get the fuck up.

556
00:45:36,733 --> 00:45:37,985
Why won't you listen to me?

557
00:45:38,068 --> 00:45:39,403
- [grunts]
- Come with me now.

558
00:45:39,486 --> 00:45:41,071
I won't say it again.

559
00:45:41,155 --> 00:45:42,614
[pants]

560
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:44,366
- [gunshot]
- [gasps]

561
00:45:46,368 --> 00:45:47,995
[gasping]

562
00:45:52,541 --> 00:45:53,834
- Andres-- [grunts]
- [gunshot]

563
00:45:53,917 --> 00:45:55,169
[body thuds]

564
00:45:55,252 --> 00:45:56,545
[Javier groans]

565
00:45:56,628 --> 00:46:00,132
[breathing heavily]

566
00:46:09,558 --> 00:46:12,561
[classical music playing]

567
00:46:42,925 --> 00:46:44,426
[door creaking]

568
00:46:54,853 --> 00:46:57,898
Diwa! Come on, stand up.
[breathing heavily]

569
00:46:59,441 --> 00:47:03,278
Come on. [grunts] Diwa! [grunts]

570
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:04,988
[straining]

571
00:47:05,072 --> 00:47:06,573
- Wake up.
- [Rebecca] Sabina.

572
00:47:08,617 --> 00:47:09,618
Ma!

573
00:47:12,371 --> 00:47:13,205
We need to go.

574
00:47:14,081 --> 00:47:14,915
Now!

575
00:47:16,083 --> 00:47:19,127
Sabina, come on. Let's go!

576
00:47:19,211 --> 00:47:21,046
- Wait. We can't leave her here.
- Huh?

577
00:47:23,423 --> 00:47:24,925
Okay. Come on.

578
00:47:25,884 --> 00:47:27,761
[women grunting]

579
00:47:44,444 --> 00:47:45,696
[coughs]

580
00:47:58,959 --> 00:47:59,835
[sniffles]

581
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:19,896
[cries softly]

582
00:48:21,440 --> 00:48:23,775
[classical music playing]

583
00:48:38,707 --> 00:48:40,417
[chains rattling]

584
00:48:44,713 --> 00:48:46,715
[creature snoring]

585
00:48:58,226 --> 00:49:00,228
[classical music continues]

586
00:49:11,239 --> 00:49:12,574
What the fuck is that?

587
00:49:12,658 --> 00:49:16,536
- [snarling]
- [Bulak gasps]

588
00:49:22,751 --> 00:49:24,002
Who the hell are you?

589
00:49:25,253 --> 00:49:26,463
What the fuck are you doing?

590
00:49:26,546 --> 00:49:28,423
Sarge, let's get out of here.

591
00:49:29,383 --> 00:49:31,259
[suspenseful music playing]

592
00:49:37,724 --> 00:49:39,726
[theme music playing]
